{%- comment -%}
  Shadow of just-the-docs's _includes/css/activation.scss.liquid.

  Emits the per-page CSS that highlights the current page's nav entry,
  unfolds its ancestor collections, and rotates their expander icons --
  the no-JS fallback that lives in the `<style id="jtd-nav-activation">`
  block in head.html. When JavaScript is enabled the theme's
  `disableHeadStyleSheets()` disables this block before applying
  `.active` classes via `activateNav()`; visitors with JS off rely on
  these rules.

  The upstream computes the page's positional path through the nav
  tree by scanning the cached site_nav HTML (~150 KB) per page, which
  costs ~11 s across the ~830-page site. This shadow consumes
  `page.nav_levels` precomputed in Ruby by
  `_plugins/nav-levels-precompute.rb` -- the same `[i, j, k, ...]`
  array the upstream Liquid algorithm would build. The output CSS is
  byte-identical to the upstream version after HTML compression.

  Data shape on `page.nav_levels`:
    Array of integers, ordered from collection-index outward:
      nav_levels[0]   = collection index (always 1 on this site;
                        the activation prefix is
                        `.site-nav > ul.nav-list:first-child`)
      nav_levels[i]   = 1-based position of the i-th ancestor in its
                        parent's sorted, nav-filtered children list,
                        for i in 1..page_level
      nav_levels.size = page_level + 1

  When `page.nav_levels` is nil (page excluded from the nav, missing
  parent reference, or otherwise unresolvable) the include falls
  through to the upstream's `activation_no_nav_link` rules.

  Selector shapes (matching the upstream output verbatim):

    Background-image removal (one rule, comma-separated parts):
      - one part per ancestor level above the page's own level
        (`prefix > li > a`, `prefix > li > ul > li > a`, ...)
      - one part at the page's own level excluding the active sibling
        (`prefix > ... > li:not(:nth-child(N)) > a`)
      - one part covering all of the page's descendants
        (`prefix > ... > li > ul > li a`)
      - plus `.site-nav > ul.nav-list:not(:first-child) a` and
        `.site-nav li.external a`

    Active link bolding:
      `prefix > li:nth-child(N1) > ul > li:nth-child(N2) > ... > a`

    Expander rotation (one part per level, comma-separated):
      `prefix > li:nth-child(N1) > ... > li:nth-child(Ni) > button svg`

    Collection unfolding (one part per level, comma-separated):
      `prefix > li.nav-list-item:nth-child(N1) > ... > ul.nav-list`
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if page.nav_levels -%}

  {%- assign nav_page_level = page.nav_levels.size | minus: 1 -%}
  {%- assign nav_page_parent_level = nav_page_level | minus: 1 -%}

  {%- capture activation_collection_prefix -%}
  .site-nav > ul.nav-list:first-child
  {%- endcapture -%}

    {% if nav_page_level >= 2 -%}
    {%- for i in (1..nav_page_parent_level) -%}
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} >
    {%- for j in (2..i) %} li > ul >
    {%- endfor %} li > a,
    {% endfor -%}
    {%- endif %}
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} >
    {%- for i in (1..nav_page_parent_level) %} li > ul >
    {%- endfor %} li:not(:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[nav_page_level] }})) > a,
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} >
    {%- for i in (1..nav_page_level) %} li > ul >
    {%- endfor %} li a {
      background-image: none;
    }

    .site-nav > ul.nav-list:not(:first-child) a,
    .site-nav li.external a {
      background-image: none;
    }

    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} > li:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[1] }})
    {%- for i in (2..nav_page_level) %} > ul > li:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[i] }})
    {%- endfor %} > a {
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    {%- if site.just_the_docs.collections %}
    .site-nav > ul.nav-category-list > li > button svg,
    {% endif -%}
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} > li:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[1] }}) > button svg
    {%- for i in (2..nav_page_level) %},
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} > li:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[1] }}) >
    {%- for j in (2..i) %} ul > li:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[j] }}) >
    {%- endfor %} button svg
    {%- endfor %} {
      transform: rotate(-90deg);
    }

    {%- if site.just_the_docs.collections %}
    .site-nav > ul.nav-category-list > li.nav-list-item > ul.nav-list,
    {% endif -%}
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} > li.nav-list-item:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[1] }}) > ul.nav-list
    {%- for i in (2..nav_page_level) %},
    {{ activation_collection_prefix }} > li.nav-list-item:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[1] }}) >
    {%- for j in (2..i) %} ul.nav-list > li.nav-list-item:nth-child({{ page.nav_levels[j] }}) >
    {%- endfor %} ul.nav-list
    {%- endfor %} {
      display: block;
    }

{%- else -%}

    .site-nav ul li a {
      background-image: none;
    }

    {%- if site.just_the_docs.collections %}
    .site-nav > ul.nav-category-list > li > button svg {
      transform: rotate(-90deg);
    }
    .site-nav > ul.nav-category-list > li.nav-list-item > ul.nav-list {
      display: block;
    }
    {%- endif %}

{%- endif -%}
